Spec: JukeBoxReconcile

Purpose:
  Own the `operator` @Reconciler lane of the @JukeBox kind: the @reconcile entry with its own
    finalizer transaction, the apply pipeline (cache upsert from `status` → running-/deleting-@Job
    guard → render-context assembly → permanent `scan.yaml`/`cronscan.yaml` Job+CronJob maintenance
    → `vynil.solidite.fr/force-scan` consumption with filter injection, Job recreation and
    post-success annotation removal), the cleanup lane (cache eviction plus warn-only CronJob/Job
    purge), and @error_policy — freezing every scan @Job/@CronJob template field contract the
    parent specs deferred here, every @Action duration of the lane, and its @Error mapping. The
    controller never
    scans and never writes `status`: scanned data reaches the cache one-way from what the spawned
    scan Jobs (agent) wrote through /common/src/jukebox.sdd.

Owns:
  ./jukebox.rs

References:
  ./lib.sdd — @Reconciler this file implements for @JukeBox, the crate-root @Error/@Result, the
    @get_client_name SSA field manager both Job patches force, and the finalizer-dispatch contract
    (this kind uses its own finalizer wrapper, not @run_with_finalizer).
  ./manager.sdd — @Context (all six fields), the @Context::cache_needs_update,
    @Context::upsert_jukebox_cache and @Context::remove_jukebox_cache call sites resolved here,
    @cache_entry_differs/@upsert_cache_entry semantics, the @Diagnostics::last_event writes, and
    the `base_context` env bake — keys `agent_image`, `log_level`, `service_account` are consumed
    by this file's templates but owned there; the scan-job rules that spec deferred land in Must.
  ./metrics.sdd — @Metrics::jukebox @count_and_measure (the @reconcile RAII measurer) and
    @reconcile_failure (the @error_policy increment).
  ./telemetry.sdd — @telemetry::get_trace_id and the @TraceId::INVALID sentinel this file guards.
  ./instance_common.sdd — @is_job_terminal, exported to this file for the scan-job guard (the one
    JukeBox tie into the instance engine); its cleanup/@upsert_job lanes are the documented
    contrast for this file's opposite error polarities.
  /common/src/jukebox.sdd — @JukeBox, @JukeBoxSpec::schedule, @JukeBoxStatus; a same-basename
    collision to flag: /common/src/jukebox.sdd and this jukebox.sdd share the basename across
    directories — that spec owns the CRD model and status mutators (`Spec: JukeBox`), this one the
    operator reconcile engine; SCAN_PACKAGE filter values follow that spec's
    @JukeBox::set_status_packages_merge `<category>`/`<category>/<name>` grammar.
  /common/src/jukebox_file.sdd — not used on this path: the file-scan variant never reaches the
    cluster; named only to exclude the engine context.
  /common/src/context.sdd — @common::context::get_client_name; this file writes SSA under the crate
    root @get_client_name of ./lib.sdd only (lib.sdd freezes the split).
  /common/src/handlebarshandler.sdd — @HandleBars `Clone` + @Deref render lane and the core partial
    registration that registers `../templates/*.hbs` minus the `.hbs` suffix, making
    `scan.yaml`/`cronscan.yaml` renderable names.
  /common/src/vynilpackage.sdd — @VynilPackage, opaque payload of the cache mirror and of tests'
    @make_pkg.

Must:
  Freeze @JUKEBOX_FINALIZER as the private `static` `&str` `jukeboxes.vynil.solidite.fr` — the
    finalizer @kube adds on the apply path and removes only after cleanup answers @Ok.
  Run the entry @reconcile in exactly this order: `#[instrument(skip(ctx, dist), fields(trace_id))]`
    span open → @telemetry::get_trace_id captured → @Span record of `trace_id` via @field::display,
    then the same record repeated under `if trace_id != @TraceId::INVALID` — a dead duplicate while
    ./telemetry.sdd stubs the getter — → @ctx.metrics.jukebox.@count_and_measure bound as `let _mes`
    so the observation covers the whole finalizer transaction → @Diagnostics::last_event :=
    @Utc::now → cluster-scope @Api::@all(@JukeBox) over @Context::client → @kube @finalizer with
    @JUKEBOX_FINALIZER dispatching @Finalizer::Apply to @Reconciler::reconcile and
    @Finalizer::Cleanup to @Reconciler::cleanup → @Err mapped to @Error::FinalizerError by boxing.
  Stamp @Diagnostics::last_event again as the first action of both @Reconciler::reconcile and
    @Reconciler::cleanup — every event therefore writes the stamp twice (entry plus body), like the
    ./instance_common.sdd wrapper lane.
  Run @Reconciler::reconcile stages in exactly this order: @tracing::debug! `Reconcilling JukeBox
    {name}` (misspelling kept) → stamp → @Context::renderer clone, @Context::client, controller ns
    from @Client::@default_namespace, @Job/@CronJob names, force-scan annotation read → gated cache
    upsert → running/deleting @Job guard → render context → permanent CronJob @Patch::Apply →
    conditional scan-@Job upsert → success debug `Reconcilling JukeBox {} Done` →
    @Action::requeue(@tokio::time::Duration::from_mins(15)).
  Compute the two workload names identically: @job_name is `scan-{@name_any}` for both the @Job
    and the @CronJob (same text, different kinds), patched through namespace-scoped @Api::@namespaced
    on @Client::@default_namespace — never the box namespace (@JukeBox is cluster-scoped), never the
    `vynil_namespace` env bake, which this file never reads.
  Read the single control annotation `vynil.solidite.fr/force-scan` as `.get(...).cloned()`, key
    presence plus value mattering per Must below; every other annotation is inert — the instance
    `suspend` annotation does not exist on this lane.
  Upsert the package cache before any guard: @ctx.cache_needs_update(@self) answered @true →
    @ctx.upsert_jukebox_cache(@self), so a `status` written by a scan Job enters the cache even when
    the guard requeues or an annotation aborts the pass; the ./manager.sdd diff/upsert rules run here
    unchanged and an unchanged status pays no write lock.
  Guard on the @Job after the cache step via @Api::@get_opt(@job_name): @Ok(Some) with
    `metadata.deletion_timestamp` set → @Action::requeue(@tokio::time::Duration::from_mins(1)) with
    no log line and no CronJob maintenance; @Ok(Some) whose @is_job_terminal answers @false →
    @tracing::info! `JukeBox {} scan job is still running, requeuing in 1 minute` and the same
    1-minute requeue; @Ok(Some) terminal → remember @job_is_terminal(`true`) and continue;
    @Ok(None) or any @Err (including a non-`NotFound` failure, indistinguishable here) →
    @job_is_terminal(`false`) and continue as if absent.
  Assemble the render context as @Context::base_context clone plus three insertions under an
    `as_object_mut` guard that silently skips all of them on a non-object @Value: `name`
    (@name_any), `job_name`, `schedule` (@JukeBoxSpec::schedule verbatim — this file never parses
    or validates the cron text; server-side CronJob acceptance is the only check).
  Maintain the CronJob on every pass that reaches it: render `{{> cronscan.yaml }}` against the
    context (@Err aborts), convert with @common::yamlhandler::@yaml_str_to_json (@Err aborts),
    @Api::@patch(@Patch::@Apply, @PatchParams::@apply(&@get_client_name()).@force()) under
    @job_name; @Err maps @Error::KubeError and aborts the pass, so an invalid schedule retries
    through @error_policy. CronJob maintenance is skipped entirely by any guard requeue, so a long
    or stuck scan delays edits to `schedule` until the job turns terminal.
  Create or recreate the scan @Job exactly when private @should_create_scan_job answers — the `const fn`
    rule `! @job_is_terminal || @force_scan.is_some()`: absent terminal @Job creates once, a present
    terminal @Job without force is never re-created (periodic rescans are the CronJob's exclusive
    duty), force-scan re-creates regardless.
  Run the force branch in this order when the annotation value is present: if the terminal @Job
    exists, foreground @Api::@delete and — only on the @either::Left echo —
    @wait_job_deleted (@Err propagates; @Err or the @either::Right confirmations skip the purge
    quietly); then @inject_package_filter; then @upsert_scan_job; then and only after success
    @remove_force_scan_annotation — the annotation stays on any earlier failure so the next pass
    retries the whole intent.
  Consume the annotation value exactly: @inject_package_filter inserts `package_filter` only when
    the value is neither `true` nor the empty string — `true`/`""` mean a full rescan Job with no
    `SCAN_PACKAGE`; any other text (free-form, typically `<category>` or `<category>/<name>` per
    /common/src/jukebox.sdd's filter grammar) is inserted verbatim and the render context injection
    affects only the direct @Job, never the CronJob template, so periodic cron scans always scan
    complete boxes.
  Run @upsert_scan_job as the @Job lane: render `{{> scan.yaml }}`, @yaml_str_to_json, forced SSA
    @Patch::@Apply under @get_client_name; a rejected patch is kept un-inspected and
    unlogged (transient or immutable-field alike) and rebuilds only when the same-call foreground
    @Api::@delete answers @either::Left — @wait_job_deleted, then @Api::@create
    (@PostParams::@default, @serde_json decode @Err → @Error::SerializationError, @Err →
    @Error::KubeError); @Err from the patch plus @Err or @either::Right from the delete silently
    returns @Ok — the pass reports success although the @Job was never updated (Tasks `[?]`,
    contrast @upsert_job in ./instance_common.sdd which maps the delete @Err to @Error::KubeError).
  Bound both waits of @wait_job_deleted at @std::time::Duration::from_secs(20) around
    @await_condition with @conditions::@is_deleted over `metadata.uid` (@unwrap_or_default on an
    absent uid), expiry → @Error::Elapsed, watch @Err → @Error::KubeWaitError; the resolved
    confirmation value is discarded.
  Remove the annotation in @remove_force_scan_annotation through cluster-scope @Api::@all(@JukeBox)
    with one @Patch::@Json document — a single `op` `remove` entry at
    `/metadata/annotations/vynil.solidite.fr~1force-scan` under @PatchParams::@default — decode
    @Err → @Error::SerializationError, @Err → @Error::KubeError.
  Run @Reconciler::cleanup in exactly this order: stamp @last_event → @ctx.remove_jukebox_cache on
    @name_any unconditionally (absent key is a silent success, ./manager.sdd) → CronJob
    @get_metadata_opt: only @Ok(Some) triggers a foreground @Api::@delete whose @Err is warned away
    as `Deleting CronJob {} failed with: {e}` and whose get @Err counts as absent → the same
    pattern for the scan @Job warning `Deleting Job {} failed with: {e}` →
    @Ok(@Action::await_change()). Cleanup never waits for any deletion to land (unlike the instance
    delete-job engine) and never removes the annotation; the finalizer releases whatever purge
    outcome happened — see Tasks `[?]` on orphans.
  Use the scan Job template (partial `scan.yaml`) verbatim as the @Job contract: @metadata.name
    `{{job_name}}`; labels exactly `app.kubernetes.io/instance` → `{{name}}`,
    `app.kubernetes.io/managed-by` → `vynil`, `vynil.solidite.fr/owner-type` → `jukebox`; no
    annotations, no ownerReferences — the @Job outlives the reconcile purely by these lanes plus
    its TTL. @spec.ttlSecondsAfterFinished `432000` and @spec.backoffLimit `3`; pod
    `restartPolicy: OnFailure`; no volumes or mounts of any kind. The single container `scan` has
    no `command` — @args exactly `box` then `scan` — @image `{{agent_image}}`, @imagePullPolicy
    `IfNotPresent`, and no `imagePullSecrets`. Env exactly: `JUKEBOX` → `{{name}}`;
    `VYNIL_NAMESPACE` via @fieldRef `metadata.namespace` (the Job's own namespace, not the
    controller env bake); `POD_NAME` via @fieldRef `metadata.name`; `RUST_BACKTRACE` → `1`;
    `LOG_LEVEL` → `{{log_level}}`; `RUST_LOG` → `info,controller=info,agent=info`; and — only when
    `package_filter` is set — `SCAN_PACKAGE` → `{{package_filter}}`. Resources: limits cpu `1000m`
    memory `1Gi`, requests cpu `50m` memory `64Mi`. Pod @securityContext
    `fsGroup`/`runAsGroup`/`runAsUser` all `65534`; @serviceAccount and @serviceAccountName both
    render `{{service_account}}`.
  Use the cronscan template (partial `cronscan.yaml`) verbatim as the @CronJob contract: @metadata
    same name and same three labels; @spec.concurrencyPolicy `Forbid`;
    @spec.successfulJobsHistoryLimit `3` and no failed-history setting (cluster default applies);
    @spec.schedule `{{schedule}}` injected as a raw unquoted YAML scalar; @spec.jobTemplate carries
    the identical container `scan` (@image `{{agent_image}}`, same @args `box scan`, same six env
    entries, same limits/requests and `65534` security context, same `{{service_account}}` pair,
    `restartPolicy: OnFailure`) with no `SCAN_PACKAGE` conditional, no `ttlSecondsAfterFinished`
    and no `backoffLimit` — cron-spawned child Jobs are named and GC'd by Kubernetes, never by
    this file, and a `SCAN_PACKAGE`-carrying force @Job never shares a name with them.
  Mirror @JukeBox `status` into the package cache one-way — the status mutators
    @JukeBox::set_status_updated, @JukeBox::set_status_failed and
    @JukeBox::set_status_packages_merge run in the agent's spawned scan Jobs per
    /common/src/jukebox.sdd; the only cluster-side @JukeBox write of this lane anywhere is the
    force-scan annotation JSON-patch.
  Fix @error_policy as `#[must_use] pub fn`: @tracing::warn! `reconcile failed for JukeBox {:?}:
    {:?}` (@Debug of `metadata.name` and of the @Error) →
    @ctx.metrics.jukebox.@reconcile_failure(@dist, @error) → two no-op @drop calls →
    @Action::requeue of @tokio::time::Duration::from_mins(5) — the single failure
    requeue of the lane, taken by every raise including @Error::FinalizerError and every discarded
    error class that still reached `?`.
  Satisfy the ./lib.rs unwrap/expect deny: every absent value rides @unwrap_or_default,
    `.cloned()` or the @either arms; no product @unwrap/@expect exists between the entry span and
    @error_policy.

Must not:
  Honor `vynil.solidite.fr/suspend` or any instance-engine annotation: force-scan is the only
    annotation this lane reads, and the reconcile body takes none to the cache, Job or CronJob
    stages when absent.
  Delete or edit the CronJob from the apply path — force-scan recreates the direct @Job only; the
    CronJob exists until cleanup removes it.
  Read tenant or instance resources: the scan Jobs touch package sources and box status, never
    @TenantInstance/@ServiceInstance/@SystemInstance objects.

Depends on:
  @kube — @Api (@all/@namespaced/@get_opt/@get_metadata_opt/@patch/@delete/@create),
    @Patch::@Apply/@Patch::@Json, @PatchParams, @DeleteParams::@foreground, @PostParams,
    @ResourceExt::@name_any, @runtime::finalizer (@finalizer/@Event), @runtime::wait::@await_condition,
    @api::conditions::@is_deleted, @runtime::controller::@Action, @Client::@default_namespace; the
    kube `3.1.0` pins are ./manager.sdd's.
  @k8s_openapi `batch/v1` @Job and @CronJob types.
  @crate root (./lib.sdd) — @Error, @Result, @JukeBox, @Reconciler, @get_client_name,
    @instance_common::@is_job_terminal, @manager::@Context, @telemetry.
  @common — @handlebarshandler::@HandleBars (clone + @Deref render), @yamlhandler::@yaml_str_to_json
    (owned by /common/src/yamlhandler.sdd as a @vynil_core re-export), the /common/src/jukebox.sdd
    model fields.
  ../templates/scan.yaml.hbs and ../templates/cronscan.yaml.hbs — render contract frozen in Must;
    the files themselves are /operator/operator.sdd-owned (`./templates/**`).
  @either — the @Api::@delete @either::Left/@either::Right echo arms both purge lanes branch on.
  @tokio::time — @Duration::@from_mins clocks of all @Actions and @timeout of the 20 s wait;
    @chrono::@Utc, @serde_json/@json, @tracing (plus the @instrument/@field/@Span attrs),
    @async_trait, @std::sync::@Arc, @opentelemetry @TraceId for the INVALID sentinel.

Exposes:
  @reconcile — `#[instrument] pub async fn(@reconcile)(@std::sync::@Arc<@JukeBox>,
    @std::sync::@Arc<@Context>) -> @Result<@Action>`; the ./manager.rs jukebox controller leg.
  @error_policy — `#[must_use] pub fn(@error_policy)(@Arc<@JukeBox>, &@Error, @Arc<@Context>) ->
    @Action`.
  @Reconciler for @JukeBox — the @Reconciler::reconcile/@Reconciler::cleanup implementation reached
    only from @reconcile's own finalizer match (./lib.sdd dispatch contract).
  Crate-private, frozen through Must/Raises/Scenarios only: @JUKEBOX_FINALIZER, @should_create_scan_job,
    @inject_package_filter, @wait_job_deleted, @upsert_scan_job, @remove_force_scan_annotation.

Accepts:
  A watch-event @Arc<@JukeBox> in any state — cluster-scoped CR, `spec.schedule` an uninterpreted
    @String, annotation values uninterpreted free text, `status` absent or arbitrary payload
    (@name_any `""` for a nameless box keys the cache write per the ./manager.sdd rule).
  @Arc<@Context> with its tokio preconditions (@RwLock awaits) and a renderer whose partial dir was
    registered by ./manager.rs @build_context — missing partials fail the first render, mid-reconcile,
    not here.
  @error_policy additionally accepts any &@Error, raising none itself.

Returns:
  @Action::requeue(@tokio::time::Duration::from_mins(1)) — deleting-timestamp guard and
    still-running guard; @Action::requeue(@tokio::time::Duration::from_mins(15)) — every completed
    apply pass; @Action::requeue(@tokio::time::Duration::from_mins(5)) — @error_policy only;
    @Action::@await_change() — cleanup only, releasing the finalizer.
  @Error::FinalizerError from @reconcile; @Ok(@())/@Err from @wait_job_deleted, @upsert_scan_job and
    @remove_force_scan_annotation; @bool from @should_create_scan_job; @() from
    @inject_package_filter (insertion or silent skip).
  Side outputs: the @last_event stamps, cache mutation, the SSA Job/CronJob writes, the annotation
    removal, the metrics run/failure increments and duration observation.

Raises:
  @Error::FinalizerError — boxed @kube finalizer transaction failure from @reconcile (the
    the @Finalizer::@Apply and @Finalizer::@Cleanup body errors ride inside it back to
    @error_policy).
  @Error::KubeError — CronJob forced patch, the rebuild @Api::@create, the JSON-patch annotation
    removal, upsert's decode-then-create leg.
  @Error::KubeWaitError and @Error::Elapsed — the two legs of @wait_job_deleted (force purge and
    rebuild purge alike, 20 s cap).
  @Error::SerializationError — the Job decode in the rebuild create and the JSON-patch document
    decode.
  @Error::Core wrapping @vynil_core::@Error::HbsRenderError (both template renders) and
    @Error::Core wrapping @vynil_core::@Error::YamlError (both conversions) — the render lane rides
    the @vynil_core engine through @Deref, so the direct-common @Error::HbsRenderError variant stays
    unused on this path while ./instance_common.sdd's Raises wording says otherwise (Tasks `[?]`).
  Laundered without an @Error: every @Api::@get_opt probe @Err reads as "no job";
    @upsert_scan_job discards its rejected patch and its own delete @Err alike (@Ok anyway); both
    cleanup deletes warn; @error_policy only warns and counts.

Handles:
  A running or foreground-terminating scan @Job — requeue-1-minute loop; `schedule` edits and every
    other pass work wait for the terminal turn (CronJob maintenance is behind the guard).
  An API error (not just `NotFound`) on the @Api::@get_opt probe — indistinguishable from absent;
    the pass continues and force-patches or rebuilds a possibly-live Job (Tasks `[?]`).
  A terminal @Job without force — untouched on the apply path, aging out via
    `ttlSecondsAfterFinished` `432000` (5 days), rescans meanwhile owned by the CronJob.
  `force-scan=true` or `force-scan=""` — full rescan recreate; `force-scan=database` or
    `force-scan=database/pg` — recreate carrying `SCAN_PACKAGE` verbatim for
    @JukeBox::@set_status_packages_merge in the agent.
  Any abort inside the force branch (delete-wait expiry, render failure, create conflict) — the
    annotation survives; the 5-minute retry re-runs the whole intent, and a
    deletion-timestamped half-deleted @Job parks on the 1-minute guard until gone, so the flow is
    re-entrant but a late @remove_force_scan_annotation failure re-scans once more before sticking.
  A base_context that is not a JSON object — all key insertions (@name/@job_name/@schedule plus
    @inject_package_filter) silently no-op and the templates render empty holes (same lane as
    ./instance_common.sdd's context guard).
  Cleanup with either workload present-but-undeleteable or with get @Err — warns twice at most,
    returns @Action::@await_change() and the finalizer releases anyway; cache eviction always
    happens first. The scan workload can therefore outlive its @JukeBox (Tasks `[?]`).
  @TraceId::INVALID — the entry records it on the span twice and the ./metrics.sdd exemplar lane
    refuses it; every shipped run takes this lane because ./telemetry.sdd stubs @get_trace_id.

Tasks:
  [x] Pure-helper and engine-entry coverage green under `cargo test -p operator`:
      @should_create_scan_job via @no_job_always_creates_scan_job,
      @terminal_job_without_force_scan_skips_job_creation,
      @terminal_job_with_force_scan_recreates_job; @inject_package_filter via
      @partial_filter_injects_package_filter, @true_value_does_not_inject_package_filter,
      @empty_value_does_not_inject_package_filter, @category_only_filter_injects_package_filter;
      engine entry lanes via @cache_updated_from_status_while_job_running (running-job requeue +
      pre-guard cache upsert) and @cleanup_removes_cache_entry (cache eviction through two `404`
      metadata probes) — @make_test_ctx is the shared @Context builder.
  [ ] Cover the guard matrix not on the two tested lanes: the deletion-timestamp requeue (no info
      line, no CronJob call), and the terminal-without-force pass that patches the CronJob and
      skips @Job creation without re-creating it.
  [ ] Cover the force-scan end-to-end: terminal-@Job foreground delete + wait, filter injection into
      the @Job render only, annotation removal strictly after creation, annotation retained on
      creation failure, and re-entrant recovery from a mid-branch wait error.
  [ ] Cover @upsert_scan_job polarities: patch @Ok; patch @Err + delete @either::Left rebuild-create; the
      silent @Ok of patch @Err + delete @Err/@either::Right; rebuild decode/map failures — @make_test_ctx
      with a @HandleBars that has the partial dir registered.
  [ ] Cover @wait_job_deleted (expiry → @Error::Elapsed, watch @Err → @Error::KubeWaitError) and
      @remove_force_scan_annotation patch body (the `~1` escaped path entry).
  [ ] Cover the frozen template rendering — render both partials against a fixture context and
      assert the Job/CronJob field sets of Must (labels, args `box scan`, env list incl. the
      `SCAN_PACKAGE` conditional, ttl `432000`, backoffLimit `3`, `65534` security context,
      `{{service_account}}` pair).
  [ ] Cover @error_policy (warn line, `jukebox_reconcile_failures_total` growth via the
      @make_test_ctx @Metrics read back the way ./metrics.sdd's `[ ]` asks) and the free-body
      @reconcile finalizer transaction incl. @Error::FinalizerError mapping — controller/finalizer
      harness needed.
  [?] Silent-upsert: @upsert_scan_job answers @Ok when both the patch and the delete failed and
      discards any patch reason unlogged — a permanently rejected @Job template can pin the lane on
      15-minute no-op passes forever. ./instance_common.sdd's @upsert_job maps the delete @Err to
      @Error::KubeError; decide one shared error polarity.
  [?] Orphan workloads: the @Job/@CronJob carry no @ownerReferences; cleanup deletes the two exact
      names warn-only and never awaits, so a failed purge or get @Err leaves a scan Job running (it
      scans on and fails status writes against the gone box) and cron children cascade only while
      the parent delete lands. Decide @ownerReference + awaited-purge ownership.
  [?] Scan-@Job privilege: it runs as `{{service_account}}` (one bake shared with install Jobs,
      uid/gid `65534`), cluster-privileged through RBAC owned outside these crates, and has no
      `imagePullSecrets` even though @JukeBoxSpec::pull_secret exists — a private AGENT_IMAGE would
      never pull. Decide a scan-dedicated @ServiceAccount and/or the pull-secret lane.
  [?] Non-`NotFound` @Api::@get_opt @Err reads as "no job", letting a blippy API make the pass force-patch
      or delete+recreate a live running scan. Decide whether wait/continue beats treat-as-absent.
  [?] @schedule is never parsed or validated here and lands unquoted in the YAML — server-side
      rejection becomes a 5-minute @error_policy loop, and structural YAML characters (`#`, `: `,
      leading indicator) in the text can rewrite the manifest shape; the model-side gap is already
      `[?]` in /common/src/jukebox.sdd. Decide where schedule validation lives.
  [?] Lifecycle asymmetry: the direct @Job gets ttl `432000` + `backoffLimit 3`, cron children get
      neither (history limits alone) — decide whether the two templates should share one retention
      story.
  [?] `RUST_LOG` is the literal `info,controller=info,agent=info` inside the `agent` image, naming
      the `controller` crate tree — looks copied from the controller container. Decide the agent
      directives.
  [?] The dead duplicate `trace_id` @Span record rides the same unreachable @TraceId::INVALID guard
      as the ./instance_common.sdd `[?]`; resolve with the ./telemetry.sdd stub decision.
  [?] @Error::HbsRenderError is never produced on this lane (renders surface as @Error::Core wrapping
      the core variant) although ./instance_common.sdd's Raises names it for the render leg —
      correct that spec's wording at its next update; not edited from here.

Done when:
  Every Scenario has a green mapped test or a decided `[?]` Task, the silent-upsert and
    orphan-workload decisions are recorded, and `cargo test -p operator`, `cargo clippy
    --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo +nightly fmt --check` and `specdd lint` are green.

Scenario: Cache refresh precedes the running-job guard
  Given a @JukeBox with a status differing from the cache and a still-running `scan-box-a` @Job
    (active, no terminal condition)
  When @Reconciler::reconcile runs
  Then the cache gains the `box-a` entry anyway and the answer is
    @Action::requeue(@tokio::time::Duration::from_mins(1)) with the info line, before any CronJob or
    @Job write
  Maps to test @cache_updated_from_status_while_job_running

Scenario: A deleting or running job defers the whole pass
  Given the named @Job with `metadata.deletion_timestamp` set
  When @Reconciler::reconcile runs
  Then the answer is the 1-minute requeue without log, CronJob patch or context work
  And the same clock answers for the still-active @Job, but with its info line; terminal-ness is
    decided solely by ./instance_common.sdd's @is_job_terminal strings
  No mapped test exists for the deleting leg; the running leg rides
    @cache_updated_from_status_while_job_running.

Scenario: Terminal job without force-scan keeps the job, not the CronJob, off the table
  Given a terminal `scan-box` @Job and no force-scan annotation
  When @Reconciler::reconcile runs
  Then the CronJob is SSA-patched with the current `schedule` yet the @Job is neither deleted nor
    re-created, and the pass closes on @Action::requeue(@tokio::time::Duration::from_mins(15))
  Maps to tests @no_job_always_creates_scan_job, @terminal_job_without_force_scan_skips_job_creation
    for the decision fn only — the pass itself is untested.

Scenario: Force-scan recreates the job, filters the render, consumes the annotation last
  Given a terminal (or absent) `scan-box` @Job annotated `vynil.solidite.fr/force-scan` with value
    `database/postgresql`
  When @Reconciler::reconcile takes the force branch
  Then the terminal @Job is foreground-deleted and awaited on the @either::Left echo, `package_filter`
    enters the @Job render context (never the CronJob), `SCAN_PACKAGE: database/postgresql` appears
    on the recreated @Job, and the JSON-patch removal of the annotation runs only after creation
    success
  And values `true` or the empty string recreate a full-scan @Job whose template renders no
    `SCAN_PACKAGE` entry
  Maps to tests @terminal_job_with_force_scan_recreates_job, @partial_filter_injects_package_filter,
    @category_only_filter_injects_package_filter, @true_value_does_not_inject_package_filter,
    @empty_value_does_not_inject_package_filter for the decisions — the end-to-end branch is untested.

Scenario: Upsert rebuild and its silence classes
  Given a scan @Job whose live spec rejects the forced SSA patch (immutable field)
  When @upsert_scan_job runs
  Then the delete-on-@either::Left rebuild chain runs — foreground delete, 20 s @is_deleted wait,
    @PostParams::@default create — surfacing @Error::Elapsed/@Error::KubeWaitError/@Error::SerializationError/@Error::KubeError
  But when the delete instead answers @Err or the @either::Right status confirmation, the whole rebuild is
    skipped and the helper still returns @Ok, pass and metrics reporting success
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Cleanup evicts the cache and best-effort purges both workloads
  Given a deleting @JukeBox `box-a` present in the package cache
  When @Reconciler::cleanup runs against a cluster where `scan-box-a` @CronJob and @Job are absent
    (`404` metadata probes)
  Then the `box-a` cache key is removed and the answer is @Action::@await_change()
  And when the resources exist, each is foreground-deleted with failures warned as
    `Deleting CronJob {} failed with: {e}` / `Deleting Job {} failed with: {e}` and the release
    happens anyway
  Maps to test @cleanup_removes_cache_entry for the all-absent leg — the warn lanes are untested.

Scenario: Every failure rides the five-minute policy
  Given any @Err from a reconcile pass — render hole, CronJob `422` schedule rejection, wait expiry,
    finalizer conflict — wrapped or direct
  When @error_policy runs
  Then one @tracing::warn! names the box name and @Error, `jukebox_reconcile_failures_total` grows
    with the @Error::metric_label child and the answer is @Action::requeue(@tokio::time::Duration::from_mins(5))
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Invalid schedule text dies at the CronJob patch, never at parse
  Given `spec.schedule` that is not a valid cron expression (e.g. `every noon`)
  When @Reconciler::reconcile renders and patches the @CronJob
  Then nothing client-side rejects it — the API's rejection returns @Error::KubeError and the lane
    retries on the 5-minute failure clock while the @Job/cache lanes of earlier passes stand
  No mapped test exists.

Example:
  Names: @JukeBox `home` → @Job name `scan-home` and @CronJob name `scan-home`, both in
    @Client::@default_namespace (in-cluster: the controller @Pod's namespace).
  Annotation semantics: `force-scan=true` → full rescan; `force-scan=database` →
    `SCAN_PACKAGE` `database`; `force-scan=database/postgresql` → same text; `force-scan=""` →
    full rescan and the annotation is still consumed and removed.
  Render context delta over `base_context`: `name`, `job_name`, `schedule`, plus conditional
    `package_filter`; templates consume `agent_image`, `log_level`, `service_account` from the bake
    (./manager.sdd) and never `vynil_namespace` or `label_key`.
